(a) All applications for a license under this article shall be submitted to the city manager, or his designee, on forms provided by the city for that purpose. All applications shall be sworn to or attested by the applicant as to the truth of material statements contained therein, and that no material information is misstated or omitted as to cause the application to be misleading or false. Prior to acceptance, the application form shall be complete as to contents and required attachments, including required inspection reports of the business premises. All applications shall be accompanied by a fee in the amount of $500.00 for processing the initial application, plus the annual license fee of $1,000.00. Licenses shall be good only for the calendar year in which issued; if a license is issued after July 1 of the current year, the initial fee shall be $500.00.
(b) Every application shall contain the following information:
(1) The full, true name of the applicant and any other names or aliases used by the applicant;
(2) Applicant's date of birth, place of birth, and social security number; if the applicant is not a U.S. citizen, but holds a visa status entitling the applicant to work in the U.S., such information shall be provided;
(3) Applicant's current address, telephone number(s) and other contact information, such as email address;
(4) All addresses at which the applicant has resided during the previous five-year period;
(5) Certified birth certificate or other legal evidence showing the applicant to be at least 21 years of age;
(6) Applicant's height, weight, color of eyes and hair;
(7) Two photographs of the applicant, suitable for passport use;
(8) Business, occupation or employment history of the applicant for the five years immediately preceding the date of application;
(9) Certified business license history of the applicant, if any, in every jurisdiction in which the applicant was subject to licensing for the five years immediately preceding the date of application;
(10) Georgia Crime Information Center report on applicant's criminal history, including arrests and pending cases, in this or any other state or territory, for the five years immediately preceding the date of application, based upon the submission of fingerprints to a law enforcement agency;
(11) Address of premises to be licensed, accompanied by plat of survey showing all structures situated thereon and a scaled floorplan of the interior of the premises to be operated as an adult business; plat shall show minimum distances, by most direct route of travel on the ground, from nearest residential zoning district boundary, occupied residence, church, school, day care center, or public park;
(12) Certified copy of deed or other title instrument showing applicant to be the owner of the real property location for which a license is sought; if the applicant is not the owner, certified copy of deed or other title instruments showing the true owner of record, accompanied by written lease agreement and contact information for the true owner;
(13) Certificate of occupancy from city building official, fire marshal and county health department showing compliance of the structure with all minimum construction codes, occupancy and use regulations, fire and life safety regulations, and health codes, based upon physical inspections conducted not more than 30 days prior to the date of submitting the application;
(14) At least five character references on applicant from individuals not related to applicant and who will not benefit financially in any way if license is granted; references shall not have been convicted of any felony or crime involving moral turpitude within the last five years prior to the date of submitting the application; full names, addresses, telephone numbers and other contact information for references shall be provided.
(c) When the applicant is a partnership, all partners shall submit personal information as required in (b) above, together with evidence of a written partnership agreement; when applicant is a corporation or other form of business entity, all individuals having five percent of more equitable ownership in the entity shall provide personal information as required in (b) above, together with evidence of the corporation's articles of incorporation, bylaws, and resolution to seek a license; upon reasonable request, the city manager may inspect and copy minutes, financial records, and other documentation of the entity needed to make a licensing decision.
(d) No license shall be issued to any applicant who:
(1) Has been convicted of a felony or crime involving moral turpitude within the five-year period immediately preceding submission of the application; for purposes hereof, a plea of nolo contendre or bond forfeiture shall be deemed a conviction;
(2) Has had a similar license for operation of an adult business revoked or suspended in this or any other jurisdiction within the past five years prior to filing application;
(3) Is legally not entitled to conduct a business in accordance with laws, regulations and ordinances of the United States, this state, or this city;
(4) Has not paid current all taxes and license fees due and owing to the city or for the premises sought to be licensed;
(5) Has made a material false statement or misrepresentation in any license or renewal application; or
(6) Has not reasonably cooperated with the city manager in the investigation of a license or renewal application.
(e) Upon receipt of an application submission, the city manager shall promptly examine the application for completeness; if a completed application has been submitted, together with a tender of the requisite fees, the city manager shall issue a provisional license, good for 45 days, under which the applicant may commence operation of the business; the city manager shall diligently investigate the applicant(s) and verify all required information, within the 45-day period; applicants may be required to appear, in person, before the city manager, for examination; on or before the 45th day, the city manager shall either (a) deny the license, stating in writing all objective grounds or lack of qualifications found, or (b) grant the license. Written notice of action shall be promptly issued to the applicant at the address shown in the application, by certified mail, return receipt requested.
(f) Whenever an application for a license is denied under this article, the aggrieved applicant shall have 30 days from the date of receipt of the written notice of denial to petition the superior court of Spalding County, Georgia, for a writ of certiorari; upon grant of the writ and motion by the petitioner for expedited hearing, the city attorney will consent to hear the matter as promptly as possible.
(g) Applications for future renewals of a license issued under this article shall be accepted by the city manager on or after October 1 of the current year for the subsequent calendar year, but not later than November 15. Renewal application forms shall be provided by the city manager and shall require the applicant to update any information as to its qualifications to possess a license, or any loss of qualifications since license issuance. All renewal applications shall be accompanied by tender of the requisite license fee for the renewal term. The fee for processing a renewal application shall be $250.00.
(h) Licenses issued under this article are not transferable. Any change in business ownership or location shall require submission of a new application based upon such change.
(Ord. No. 07-07, § 1, 8-28-2007)

